title: The Party Line
subtitle: Move the party's line on the war and the government.
card-image: img/cards/ideology.svg?v=2
new-page: true
is-card: true
tags: party_affairs
view-if: ideology_timer <= 0
on-arrival: month_actions += 1; ideology_timer = 4

[? if player_party = 'menshevik' : The party has no single line. [? if bol_regime = 0 and at_war = 1 : The Revolutionary Defencists want to defend the revolution against the Kaiser and keep the alliance with the liberals. ?][? if bol_regime = 0 and at_war = 0 : The Revolutionary Defencists want an alliance of all the democrats, the liberals included. ?][? if bol_regime = 1 : The Revolutionary Defencists want the Constituent Assembly restored, and no truce with the Bolshevik dictatorship. ?][? if intl_gone = 0 and bol_regime = 0 : The Internationalists want an immediate general peace and a government of the socialists alone. ?][? if intl_gone = 0 and bol_regime = 1 : The Internationalists want a legal opposition inside the soviets, and no part in any armed struggle against them. ?] ?][? if player_party = 'sr' : The party has no single line. [? if rightdef_gone = 0 and at_war = 1 : The Right SRs want the war carried on and the coalition kept. ?][? if rightdef_gone = 0 and at_war = 0 : The Right SRs want a democratic front against the Bolsheviks, with anyone who will join it. ?] Chernov's Centre wants a defensive war and a quick road to a general peace, and the land now. [? if intl_gone = 0 and lsr_split = 0 : The Left SRs want an immediate peace, and no more compromise with the liberals. ?][? if intl_gone = 0 and lsr_split = 1 : The Left Centre wants the party to make its peace with the soviets. ?] ?][? if player_party = 'lsr' : The party has no single line. Spiridonova and Kamkov's leadership wants the land to the peasants and the soviets to the villages, [? if at_war = 1 : and an end to the war. ?][? if at_war = 0 : and an end to the grain requisitions in the villages. ?][? if intl_gone = 0 : The pro-Bolshevik wing wants to stand beside Lenin at any price. ?][? if rightdef_gone = 0 and lsr_in_gov = 1 : The pro-coalition wing around Natanson and Kolegaev wants to keep the commissariats and the alliance. ?][? if rightdef_gone = 0 and lsr_in_gov = 0 and bol_regime = 1 : The pro-coalition wing around Natanson and Kolegaev wants the party back in the Council of People's Commissars. ?][? if rightdef_gone = 0 and lsr_in_gov = 0 and bol_regime = 0 : The pro-coalition wing around Natanson and Kolegaev wants an alliance with the Bolsheviks and a share of power. ?] ?][? if at_war = 0 : The war with Germany is over; the question is now how to treat the Bolshevik state. ?]

- @right: Move toward [+ rlbl +].
- @defencist: Move toward [+ dlbl +].
- @intl: Move toward [+ ilbl +].
- @balance: Hold the middle and calm all wings.
- @easy_discard

@right
view-if: rightdef_strength > 0
on-arrival: {!
RO.fac(Q, 'rightdef', 5, -3);
RO.fac(Q, 'defencist', -1, 2);
RO.fac(Q, 'intl', -4, 8);
Q.war_line += 2;
RO.add(Q, {rel_kad: 3});
!}

The line hardens [? if at_war = 1 : toward war to victory ?][? if at_war = 0 : against the Bolsheviks ?] and toward the liberals. [? if intl_gone = 0 : [+ flabel_intl +] are alarmed, and some of their younger members are looking at Lenin's paper. ?]

@defencist
on-arrival: {!
RO.fac(Q, 'defencist', 5, 0);
RO.fac(Q, 'rightdef', 2, -2);
RO.fac(Q, 'intl', -3, 6);
Q.war_line += 1;
RO.add(Q, {rel_kad: 3, rel_ally: 1});
!}

The majority is pleased. [? if intl_gone = 0 : [+ flabel_intl +] issued a statement of regret. ?]

@intl
view-if: intl_strength > 0
on-arrival: {!
RO.fac(Q, 'intl', 5, -6);
RO.fac(Q, 'defencist', -3, 4);
RO.fac(Q, 'rightdef', -2, 6);
Q.war_line -= 1;
RO.add(Q, {rel_kad: -3, rel_lsr: 2, rel_bol: 2});
!}

The left wing is happy. [? if rightdef_gone = 0 : [+ flabel_rightdef +] are not, and have begun to write letters to the newspapers. ?]

@balance
on-arrival: {!
for (var f of Q.factions) { RO.fac(Q, f, 0, -3); }
!}

A carefully worded resolution satisfied nobody and offended nobody. For now.
